Lock screen: up before the computer sleeps

With lockBeforeSleep, the shell asked for the lock screen when logind said
the computer was about to sleep, but nothing made logind wait for it, so
it could suspend first and show the desktop for a moment on waking. Hold a
logind "delay" inhibitor for sleep, and let go of it once the lock screen
is up (WlSessionLock.secure), right away when it is already up or
lockBeforeSleep is off; take it again on waking. logind waits at most
InhibitDelayMaxSec (5 s) if the lock never comes up.

